## Read before your first edit

1. `docs/README.md` — the standards hierarchy and what each `status` means.
2. The documents for the layers your change touches. A rule ending ` _(applies to: …)_` binds
   only components of those kinds (`service`, `daemon`, `cli`, `library`, `ui`, `batch`, listed
   in `docs/03-architecture/system.md`); a `not-applicable` document has no rules here. Only `ratified` documents are binding.
   A `proposed` document is a default not yet adopted; a `not-started` one has no rules —
   **never infer a rule from it, ask.**
3. For implementation work: the story spec and its parent feature spec
   (`docs/17-specs/spec-lifecycle.md`).{% if 'user-interface' in packs %} For interface work, also `DESIGN.md`
   (the visual identity, generated from the token source; change the tokens, never this file).{% endif %}
4. `docs/16-ai/` — what you may do on your own, what needs approval, and what is prohibited.

