## Agents

Role prompts for delegated work live in `.agents/agents/*.md`. Hand the file's body to a
subagent verbatim, followed by the task. Model choice follows `docs/16-ai/model-routing.md`.

## Checks

**Requires Node ≥ 20** — the baseline's checks, hooks and tools run on it regardless of the
project's own stack (`node --version`).

```sh
node scripts/check.mjs       # everything CI runs on the docs and adapters
```

Git hooks (`.githooks/`) run the same checks. Enable them once per clone:
`git config core.hooksPath .githooks`. Never bypass them (`--no-verify`).

- `scripts/checks/*.mjs` are check plugins run by `check.mjs`, including a secret scan. A false
  positive goes in `.baseline/secrets-allowlist.txt`, never a bypass.
- `scripts/guards/` holds tool-neutral guards (protected documents, dangerous git commands) that any
  AI tool's hooks can call.

## Workflow and tools

- `docs/workflow.yaml` declares the spec chain — feature spec → story → start → implement → PR →
  judge — and the skill that runs each stage.
- Work items go through `node scripts/tracker/cli.mjs` only (`--help` lists the verbs). There is no
  delete.
- Open pull requests with `node scripts/pr/open-pr.mjs`, which refuses a body that does not follow
  the template.

## Working rules

- Questions to the user are batched, numbered, and each carries a recommended default.
- A decision with a real alternative is recorded as an ADR (`docs/04-adr/`), via the `new-adr`
  skill.
- Never edit a `ratified` document or an `accepted` ADR without the user's explicit approval;
  changing one follows `docs/04-adr/README.md`.
- Commits follow Conventional Commits (`docs/14-git/git.md`). Agent-authored commits carry a
  `Co-Authored-By` trailer naming the agent.
- Put scratch output outside the repository, or in `.agents/out/` (ignored). Never leave notes at
  the repository root.
